KuberNow - Privacy Policy
Effective date: November 22, 2026
Last updated: November 22, 2026

1. Who we are and scope
This policy describes how KuberNow ("KuberNow," "we," "us," or "our"), the developer of the KuberNow: My Money Journey app, handles personal information in its financial education application, website, and related services (the "Service"). It applies to the app as distributed on Google Play, the Amazon Appstore, and any other store where it is offered.
Contact for privacy questions and requests: Amit@AmericaMaGujarati.com
Account and data deletion page: https://github.com/amitpatelcontract/privacypolicy/blob/master/KuberNowDeleteAccount

2. Summary
- KuberNow is a financial education app. It does not connect to your bank, brokerage, or credit accounts, does not move money, and does not ask for account numbers or passwords.
- We collect only what is needed to run the app: your account details, the learning progress and financial estimates you choose to enter, purchase status, and technical/diagnostic data.
- We do not sell your personal information and do not share it for targeted (cross-context behavioral) advertising. The app does not show third-party ads.
- Data is encrypted in transit. You can request deletion of your account and data at any time (see section 9).

3. Information you provide
Depending on the features you use, we may collect:
- Account information: name, email address, sign-in identifier (for example, from Google Sign-In or email sign-in), and language preferences.
- Financial estimates you choose to enter: such as income, expenses, savings, assets, debts, goals, and calculator assumptions. These are self-reported estimates used for educational illustrations. You may use rounded or approximate amounts.
- Learning activity: lessons completed, quiz answers, saved tasks, reminders, goals, and preferences.
- AI feature inputs and outputs: questions or text you submit to AI-powered features and the responses generated (see section 6).
- Communications: support emails, feedback, and other messages you send us.
- Purchase information: subscription status, product purchased, and transaction or order identifiers. We do not receive or store your full payment card details; payments are processed by Google Play or Amazon.
Please do not submit bank or card numbers, passwords, Social Security or other government ID numbers, or other sensitive information that is not needed for the lesson or feature you are using.

4. Information collected automatically
When you use online features, the Service and its providers may collect:
- App activity: screens viewed, features used, and in-app events.
- App info and performance: crash logs, diagnostics, app version, and performance data.
- Device and identifiers: device model, operating system version, language, approximate location derived from IP address (country or region level), Firebase installation ID, and push-notification token.
We do not collect precise location, contacts, photos, files, microphone, or camera data. Information stored only on your device is not received by us unless it is submitted or synchronized through a Service feature.

5. How we use information
We use information to:
- Create and maintain your account and sync your progress.
- Provide lessons, calculators, checklists, reminders, and educational examples based on your inputs.
- Provide AI-powered explanations when you use those features.
- Process and verify purchases and subscriptions.
- Send service notifications and, if you opt in, reminders (you can turn notifications off in device settings).
- Respond to support requests and feedback.
- Understand usage, fix crashes, and improve the Service.
- Protect security, prevent fraud and abuse, and meet legal obligations.
We do not use your financial inputs to make credit, lending, insurance, or employment decisions, and we do not use them to market third-party financial products to you.

6. Service providers we use
We share information only with providers that help us operate the Service, and only what they need for that work:
- Google Firebase (Google LLC): authentication, cloud database and storage, analytics (Google Analytics for Firebase), crash reporting (Crashlytics), and push notifications (Cloud Messaging). Google privacy policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- App stores and billing: Google Play Billing and Amazon Appstore In-App Purchasing process payments and subscriptions under their own privacy policies. If we use a subscription-management service to verify purchases, it receives purchase identifiers and an app user ID only.
- AI model providers: when you use an AI-powered feature, the text you submit (and any information you include in it, such as financial estimates) is sent to a third-party AI model provider to generate a response. We use these providers under their business/API terms and do not permit them to sell your information or use it for advertising. AI responses are educational and may be inaccurate (see the Terms). Do not include names, account numbers, or other identifying details in AI questions.
We may also disclose information to comply with law or valid legal process, to investigate fraud or security incidents, to protect the rights and safety of users or others, or as part of a merger, acquisition, or sale of the business, subject to applicable law and notice.
We do not sell personal information, do not share it for cross-context behavioral advertising, and do not give your financial inputs to banks, lenders, brokers, insurers, or other financial companies.

7. Security
Information is encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS) and stored with Google Cloud/Firebase, which encrypts data at rest. Access is limited to what is needed to operate and support the Service, and is protected by authentication and security rules. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work to protect your information and will notify you of a breach where required by law.

8. Retention
- Account, learning, and financial-estimate data: kept while your account is active. Deleted within 30 days after a verified deletion request, or after 24 months of account inactivity.
- AI feature inputs and outputs: kept only as long as needed to provide the feature and your history; deleted with your account.
- Analytics data: retained under our Google Analytics for Firebase settings (no longer than 14 months).
- Crash and diagnostic data: retained by Firebase Crashlytics for up to 90 days.
- Support correspondence: up to 24 months after the request is resolved.
- Purchase and transaction records: kept as long as required for tax, accounting, and legal purposes (generally up to 7 years). These are held mainly by Google Play or Amazon.
- Backups: deleted data may remain in encrypted backups for up to 90 days until overwritten.

9. Your choices and rights
Delete your account and data: Email Amit@AmericaMaGujarati.com from the email address on your account with the subject "Delete my KuberNow account." You can also request deletion of specific data (for example, only your financial estimates or AI history) without deleting your account. Full instructions: https://github.com/amitpatelcontract/privacypolicy/blob/master/KuberNowDeleteAccount
Access and correction: Email us to request a copy of your data or to correct it. Many details can also be edited in the app.
Notifications: You can turn off notifications in device settings.
Depending on where you live, you may have additional rights, such as to know what we collect, access, correct, delete, or port your data; to opt out of sale, sharing, targeted advertising, or profiling (we do none of these); to withdraw consent; to appeal a decision about your request; and to complain to a data protection authority. We will verify your identity before acting on a request, respond within the time required by law (generally within 30 to 45 days), and will not discriminate against you for exercising your rights. You may use an authorized agent where the law allows.
For users in the EEA, UK, or Switzerland: we process information to perform our contract with you (providing the Service), based on our legitimate interests (security, analytics, and improvement), with your consent (optional notifications and where otherwise required), and to meet legal obligations.
Uninstalling the app or deleting your account does not cancel a subscription. Cancel through Google Play or the Amazon Appstore.

10. International processing
Information may be processed in the United States and other countries where we or our providers operate. Where required, we rely on appropriate safeguards, such as Standard Contractual Clauses, for international transfers.

11. Children
The Service is intended for adults 18 and older and is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from anyone under 18. If you believe a child has provided personal information, contact us and we will delete it.

12. Third-party sites and services
External websites, app stores, sign-in providers, and payment services have their own privacy policies. Viewing this policy on GitHub is also subject to GitHub's privacy practices.

13. Changes to this policy
We may update this policy. We will change the "Last updated" date and, for material changes, notify you in the app or by email and obtain consent where required.

